{"text": " You wake up in 1661 in Stockholm. The harbor's frozen and a sledge scrapes past your window, loaded with copper. Did you know that Sweden's biggest coin weighed almost 20 kilos? It's a copper plate. You don't put it in your pocket. You put it on a cart, so a banker called Johann Palmstruck has an idea. Leave your copper at his bank and take a sheet of paper instead. It says your copper is waiting for you. These are the first real bank notes in Europe. So what is money now? A promise written on paper. Remember that word promise. It comes back at the end. People love the notes. So the bank prints more and lends more than it has copper to pay back. When people come for their copper, it isn't there. The bank fails. Palmstruck has sentenced to death. He spared and dies a few years later. Paper only works while people believe in it. And in the next century, one man will push that belief further than anyone ever had.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.88, "text": " You wake up in 1661 in Stockholm.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 3165, 31537, 294, 38730, 13, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13567663983600894, "compression_ratio": 1.5223880597014925, "no_speech_prob": 0.037937868386507034, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.14, "probability": 0.7258148193359375}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.3, "probability": 0.9826686382293701}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.3, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.99812251329422}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.6, "probability": 0.9880803823471069}, {"word": " 1661", "start": 0.6, "end": 1.74, "probability": 0.9585548341274261}, {"word": " in", "start": 1.74, "end": 2.44, "probability": 0.6392664909362793}, {"word": " Stockholm.", "start": 2.44, "end": 2.88, "probability": 0.9790482521057129}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 3.62, "end": 6.44, "text": " The harbor's frozen and a sledge scrapes past your window,", "tokens": [50544, 440, 36947, 311, 12496, 29